// DISABLE_NATIVE: targetFamily=MINGW


// KT-54330 window, sibling of the corpus case inline/privateClassDefaultCtorStubLinkage (the
// regular-class $default ctor stub): here the defaulted construction goes through a private
// VALUE CLASS, so the unmarked chain additionally crosses the value-class static constructor.
//
// The internal inline g is inlined into main (a friend module); through the private inline
// bridge probe (the frontend forbids naming a private-in-file type directly in a non-private
// inline body) the inlined body constructs V with its defaulted argument. In main's per-file
// cache the construction is lowered to the synthetic $default static constructor
// V#<constructor>#static(String?, Int, DefaultConstructorMarker?) and referenced as an
// external symbol, but lib1's per-file cache emits that stub with LLVM internal linkage:
// CacheInfoBuilder.trackCallees (CacheInfoBuilder.kt) marks only the real constructor
// V.<init>(String) with isCalledFromExportedInlineFunction, and ContextUtils.linkageOf
// propagates the flag only through irFunction.originalConstructor (set solely by
// ConstructorsLowering), while the stub carries only defaultArgumentsOriginalFunction
// (DefaultArgumentFunctionFactory) and the value-class static constructor built by
// Autoboxing's getLoweredInlineClassConstructor copies neither - both fall back to
// themselves, where the flag is not set. The link fails with an undefined symbol while the
// same klibs link and answer "V(s=five)" without incremental compilation.
//
// Harness note: the "clean" reference link also enables incremental compilation (with a fresh
// cache), so this from-scratch IC-only defect fails that link too. The harness's non-IC link
// exonerates the program, and the run is reported as BUG with IC_ONLY_LINK_FAILURE.

MODULES: lib1, main

STEP 0:
    libs: lib1, main
